  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Temperature is measured using two different scales. The formula for changing the temperature in degrees Fahrenheit (${}^\\circ\\mathrm{F}$) to degrees Celsius (${}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$) is $C=\\frac{5}{9}(F-32)$, where $C$ is the temperature in ${}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ and $F$ is the temperature in ${}^\\circ\\mathrm{F}$.\n\nFind the temperature in ${}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ corresponding to a temperature of:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$100^\\circ\\mathrm{F}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$37\\frac{7}{9}\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\frac{5}{9}(100-32)\\\\C&=\\frac{5}{9}\\times68\\\\C&=\\frac{340}{9}\\\\C&=37\\frac{7}{9}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe temperature is $37\\frac{7}{9}\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$212^\\circ\\mathrm{F}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$100^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\frac{5}{9}(212-32)\\\\C&=\\frac{5}{9}\\times180\\\\C&=100\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe temperature is $100^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$0^\\circ\\mathrm{F}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-17\\frac{7}{9}\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\frac{5}{9}(0-32)\\\\C&=\\frac{5}{9}\\times(-32)\\\\C&=-\\frac{160}{9}\\\\C&=-17\\frac{7}{9}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe temperature is $-17\\frac{7}{9}\\,{}^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$-40^\\circ\\mathrm{F}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-40^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}C&=\\frac{5}{9}\\bigl((-40)-32\\bigr)\\\\C&=\\frac{5}{9}\\times(-72)\\\\C&=-40\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe temperature is $-40^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
